# Cursor Rules — AI API Radar UI Freeze

## Default: Do Not Touch UI
Changing visual appearance is FORBIDDEN by default. UI changes require explicit prior justification and user confirmation.

## Explicitly Forbidden
- Global CSS files or theme tokens
- Header / Footer visual structure
- CTA button styles or colors
- 404 page visual design
- Color palette, typography, spacing
- Any new UI frameworks or animation libraries
- Any new design system tokens

## Explicitly Allowed
- Adding new content/data to `src/data/pages.ts`
- Adding new pages to `pages.ts` (with proper CTAs)
- Updating text content within existing components (no style changes)
- Reusing existing CSS classes/components for new content
- Updating `src/pages/index.astro` text content (not visual structure)
- Modifying sitemap/llms/robots scripts
- Adding validation scripts
- Updating metadata in existing components (title, description, H1 text)

## If UI Change Is Absolutely Necessary
1. Stop immediately
2. Report the reason
3. Get explicit user confirmation before proceeding
4. Document the exception in the completion report

## Layout Components
- `src/components/Layout.astro` — data passthrough only, no visual changes
- `src/components/SeoHead.astro` — extend for new meta fields only, do not break existing SEO basics
- `src/components/CTA.astro` — data changes only, no style changes

## What "UI Frozen" Means
The site must look identical before and after any content/data changes. Only content text and page data may differ — colors, fonts, spacing, shadows, animations, layout structure must stay the same.
